{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/770153-soul-pact-inflating-trick","id":770153,"title":"Soul Pact inflating trick?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-20T11:22:28-08:00","id":770153,"title":"Soul Pact inflating trick?","content":"So, say a Demon gets a Soul Pact out of someone. From that point on, they can claim the target as a Cover - and every relationship the person has, at the time they are claimed. Could a Demon then engage in repeated lesser Pacts, taking elements from the first target in exchange for benefits and holding the elements, only to reintegrate them back into the Cover once they claim the person? Then they would get, essentially, everything the person was <i>plus</i> all the benefits they derived from the other Pacts (provided those Benefits were social or positional). Or, free bonuses, provided they can convince a dupe to keep making Pacts.<br /> <br /> Seems like something of a systems exploit (pun intended, though it does seem in theme with Demon).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T11:34:00-08:00","id":770159,"title":"","content":"Rules as written don't cover it directly, but I'd definitely call that degrading the potential value of the soul pact. You're kind of buying this person's soul on credit \u2013 the lesser pacts give you elements of their life early, but you're taking them out of the &quot;account&quot; that you're already entitled to take in a lump sum whenever you want. Or in other words, if, say, you've got a dude whose life is worth Cover 5, and you take two dots of Cover worth of pacts out of him, then when you cash in the soul pact you're only getting Cover 3 out of it. You can save your cake for later or you can eat some of it now, but the cake will not grow back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T11:50:35-08:00","id":770175,"title":"","content":"I see what you are saying. Technically, when you cash in a Soul Pact, you get a Cover of the target/signer/victim's Integrity, which subsequent Pacts <i>need</i> not affect. Juicing them up with Resources, Status, et al, then claiming them and adding back in all that they lost (mechanically boosting the Cover up higher then when you &quot;got&quot; it) certainly looks like cheating. It may be mitigated, somewhat, by the inherent risk you are taking by playing this game long term. But it is hardly more risk than just simply not cashing out a Soul Pact immediately.<br /> <br /> A potential problem with the above I can see is book-keeping (tracking whose trade out what elements of their &quot;soul&quot; and how much). Especially since there is no indicator on the person that their &quot;soul&quot; is &quot;damaged goods&quot;. Maybe refine it into: Pacts (other than Soul Pacts) cause (or at least risk) Integrity loss commensurate to their Cover value? Then, Pacts reduce the target's Integrity, organically reducing the value of the resultant Soul Pact. As far as justifying the Integrity cost/risk on the signer's side - well, they are trading away a portion of their &quot;existence&quot;; isn't that worth a Breaking Point?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 11-20-2015, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T12:34:55-08:00","id":770205,"title":"","content":"That's what I meant when I said rules as written don't cover it directly \u2013 it's a situation where the value of the Cover ought to be degraded, but in a way that doesn't necessarily align with the quick measure of tagging the Cover value to Integrity. I wouldn't make repeated pacts with a demon breaking points in and of themselves (though certainly there could be situations where they would be). I'd just have this be a quirky situation where you get back less than the signatory's Integrity in Cover dots.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T14:02:37-08:00","id":770272,"title":"","content":"Well do remember that Demons only gain access to merits and abilities though Legend, or buy buying them themselves with their own points.<br /> <br /> And I don't see that as being too different than how pacts already work when you make someone a cult leader- you can give someone a sweet deal on pacts and in return they become your super deluxe cult leader.<br /> <br /> So I think a demon double dipping advantages through pacts is rules as intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T14:30:08-08:00","id":770293,"title":"","content":"Isn't this pretty much the same as doing the lesser Pacts first and then a Soul Pact? A situation specifically called out as normal in the book. The only difference being that you are holding on to the lesser pacts rather than patching them in or building a patch-job out of them until after you cash in the Soul Pact. Which is a reasonable enough of a downside that it seems fine. Especially when combined with what StSword said about merits and and stuff with Legend.<br /> <br /> Also, too much awkward Pacting draws plenty of scrutiny from the G-M. Both directly and from the lesser Pacts only affecting the direct targets, so inviting scrutiny from other mortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T08:33:52-08:00","id":772330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/770153-soul-pact-inflating-trick?p=770175#post770175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see what you are saying. Technically, when you cash in a Soul Pact, you get a Cover of the target/signer/victim's Integrity</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you do not. Cover resultant from a Soul Pact is equal to the Demon's Primum plus successes on their Wits + Manipulation roll to call the Pact in, and has nothing to do with the target's Integrity.<br /> <br /> More on topic, it's also impossible to reduce this number by taking elements of their life early, so feel free.<br /> <br /> That said, once you call in the Soul Pact, any lesser pacts you had with them may become invalid - you can't steal relationships from yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 11-23-2015, 11:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T09:13:54-08:00","id":772356,"title":"","content":"Huh, you're right. I don't know why I had it in my head that it was Integrity.<br /> <br /> The point was more: Assets from the Pact grant to person Skills, Merits, etc. While you can't take the Merits, the social ones <i>are</i> tied to relationships (usually). They may lose the corresponding effectiveness that the Merit granted, but you still have more relationships to leverage, in addition to those the signer Pact'ed away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 11-23-2015, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T09:37:19-08:00","id":772372,"title":"","content":"It's also important to remember, as one of the other posters alluded, that a pact doesn't have to be cashed in immediately. I might take a terrible childhood trauma from Johnny with Pact A and an ex-boyfriend from Sally with Pact B. If I apply neither until I have enough backstory to create a person (enough Cover Experiences), then I can become Sergio: a man from a troubled home that has become somewhat unreliable since The Break Up. A string of failed relationships afterwards has only perpetuated this cycle.<br /> <br /> Remember that Demons\u200b trade in Pacts as well. It's not unheard of for Mr. Needle to trade addictions for favors.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is just my bright, shiny two cents.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing. I try not to argue in forums. It's like pouring concrete in a river. It doesn't get you anywhere in the short term and it poisons the environment long term.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2668-asmenedas","name":"Asmenedas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2668_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T09:57:32-08:00","id":772381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/770153-soul-pact-inflating-trick?p=772356#post772356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh, you're right. I don't know why I had it in my head that it was Integrity.<br /> <br /> The point was more: Assets from the Pact grant to person Skills, Merits, etc. While you can't take the Merits, the social ones <i>are</i> tied to relationships (usually). They may loses the corresponding effectiveness that the Merit granted, but you still have more relationships to leverage, in addition to those the signer Pact'ed away.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think most of the players in my games have taken advantage of this and I see nothing wrong with it. You're strengthening the Cover for when you finally take it over. Seems pretty thematic to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T20:47:45-08:00","id":776975,"title":"","content":"Yeah, if you're a drug dealer you expose prospective clients to pot first, not meth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}